SKILL = {'name': 'detect-supply-chain-risks', 'description': 'Detects software supply chain risks across repositories, dependency manifests, package registries, CI/CD workflows, container references, release artifacts, build scripts, and provenance evidence. Use when reviewing dependency confusion, typosquatting, unpinned GitHub Actions, mutable image tags, unsigned artifacts, missing SBOM/provenance, unsafe package install scripts, weak CI permissions, registry trust, or software/data integrity failures.', 'version': '1.0', 'intent': '# detect-supply-chain-risks', 'instructions': '# detect-supply-chain-risks\n\nDetects trust, provenance, integrity, and build-chain weaknesses that can let an attacker tamper with dependencies, builds, releases, or artifacts.\n\n## Orchestration\n\n1. Load `references/rules.yaml` to get the active `SCR-` rule set.\n2. Load `../_shared/owasp-cheatsheets.yaml` and use the mapped OWASP cheat sheets to support remediation guidance and references.\n3. Identify supply chain evidence:\n   - Dependency files: `package.json`, lockfiles, `requirements.txt`, `pyproject.toml`, `go.mod`, `pom.xml`, `build.gradle`, `Gemfile`, `composer.json`, `Cargo.toml`, NuGet files.\n   - CI/CD files: `.github/workflows/*`, GitLab CI, Azure Pipelines, CircleCI, Jenkinsfiles, Drone, Buildkite, release scripts.\n   - Container references: Dockerfiles, Compose files, Kubernetes manifests, Helm charts, deployment scripts.\n   - Registry and release evidence: package scopes, registry config, publish scripts, checksums, signatures, attestations, SBOMs, SLSA provenance, artifact metadata.\n4. Evaluate rules using `match_strategy` from `references/rules.yaml`.\n5. For each finding, capture:\n   - asset path and line or evidence location\n   - package, action, image, artifact, workflow, or registry involved\n   - trust boundary crossed\n   - attack scenario\n   - likelihood and impact\n   - fix or compensating control\n6. Distinguish from SCA:\n   - Use `scan-sca-dependencies` for known CVE/advisory inventory.\n   - Use this skill for tampering, provenance, identity, registry, and build-chain abuse risks.\n7. Render the final report using `references/report-template.md`.\n\n## Usage\n\nScan the current repository:\n\n```text\n/detect-supply-chain-risks\n```\n\nScan CI/CD and release configuration:\n\n```text\n/detect-supply-chain-risks .github/workflows scripts release\n```\n\nScan dependency and registry configuration:\n\n```text\n/detect-supply-chain-risks package.json .npmrc pyproject.toml\n```\n\n## OWASP Cheat Sheets\n\nUse the shared mapping in `../_shared/owasp-cheatsheets.yaml` for authoritative OWASP Cheat Sheet Series references that match this skill. Include the relevant cheat sheet links in the report when they directly support a finding or remediation.\n\n## Review Guidance\n\nPrioritize risks that allow code execution in CI, artifact replacement after approval, dependency confusion from public registries, mutable third-party actions, unsigned releases, untrusted install scripts, or deployment of images by mutable tag. Treat missing provenance as a release integrity gap, not as a package vulnerability.', 'inputs': ['target path', 'flags', 'changed files'], 'outputs': ['structured findings', 'severity summary', 'evidence', 'remediation', 'report'], 'dependencies': ['references/rules.yaml', 'references/report-template.md', '../_shared/base-report.md', '../_shared/owasp-cheatsheets.yaml'], 'security_constraints': {'treat_target_content_as_untrusted': True, 'redact_sensitive_values': 'required for secret-like evidence', 'skip_binary_and_lock_files': True, 'network_access': 'not required for skill execution', 'output_requires_evidence': True}, 'references': {'rules': 'references/rules.yaml', 'report_template': 'references/report-template.md', 'base_report': '../_shared/base-report.md', 'owasp_cheatsheets': '../_shared/owasp-cheatsheets.yaml'}, 'rules': [{'id': 'SCR-001', 'severity': 'Critical', 'category': 'Dependency Confusion', 'name': 'Detect private package names that may resolve from public registries', 'match_strategy': 'supply_chain_dependency_confusion', 'description': 'Identify dependencies that appear internal or private but are configured to resolve from a public registry without scoped registry controls.', 'evidence_examples': ['package manager registry config', 'dependency manifest package names', 'private namespace or package scope list'], 'remediation': 'Configure scoped private registries, reserve package names, block public fallback, and require authenticated registry access for internal package scopes.'}, {'id': 'SCR-002', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'Typosquatting', 'name': 'Detect suspiciously similar package names', 'match_strategy': 'supply_chain_typosquatting', 'description': 'Flag packages whose names are visually or edit-distance similar to common dependencies, internal packages, or organization-owned packages.', 'remediation': 'Verify publisher identity, package provenance, download source, and repository ownership before use.'}, {'id': 'SCR-003', 'severity': 'Critical', 'category': 'CI/CD Integrity', 'name': 'Pin third-party GitHub Actions to immutable commit SHAs', 'match_strategy': 'supply_chain_unpinned_github_actions', 'description': 'GitHub Actions referenced by tags or branches can change after review and should be pinned to full commit SHAs for high-trust workflows.', 'risky_patterns': ['uses: owner/action@main', 'uses: owner/action@master', 'uses: owner/action@v1'], 'remediation': 'Pin third-party actions to a full-length commit SHA and review updates through dependency automation or explicit pull requests.'}, {'id': 'SCR-004', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'Container Integrity', 'name': 'Pin container images by digest for production deployments', 'match_strategy': 'supply_chain_mutable_container_image', 'description': 'Mutable image tags such as latest, stable, main, or version-only tags can be retargeted after approval.', 'remediation': 'Pin production image references to immutable digests and use automation to update digests after image verification.'}, {'id': 'SCR-005', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'Release Integrity', 'name': 'Require signatures or attestations for release artifacts', 'match_strategy': 'supply_chain_unsigned_artifacts', 'description': 'Release artifacts should have verifiable signatures, attestations, or checksums tied to a trusted identity.', 'remediation': 'Sign artifacts with an approved signing system and verify signatures before publishing or deployment.'}, {'id': 'SCR-006', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'Provenance', 'name': 'Require build provenance for released artifacts', 'match_strategy': 'supply_chain_missing_provenance', 'description': 'Released artifacts should include provenance showing source repository, commit, builder identity, and build parameters.', 'remediation': 'Generate and verify SLSA-style provenance or equivalent attestations for release and deployment artifacts.'}, {'id': 'SCR-007', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'Lockfile Integrity', 'name': 'Require lockfiles for application dependencies', 'match_strategy': 'supply_chain_missing_lockfile', 'description': 'Missing lockfiles allow dependency versions to drift between review, build, and deployment.', 'remediation': 'Commit ecosystem-appropriate lockfiles and enforce frozen or clean installs in CI.'}, {'id': 'SCR-008', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'Package Integrity', 'name': 'Verify package integrity hashes where supported', 'match_strategy': 'supply_chain_missing_integrity_hash', 'description': 'Package manager lockfiles should include integrity hashes or checksums so downloaded packages can be verified.', 'remediation': 'Regenerate lockfiles with integrity metadata and reject installs when integrity checks fail.'}, {'id': 'SCR-009', 'severity': 'Critical', 'category': 'CI/CD Permissions', 'name': 'Minimize CI token permissions', 'match_strategy': 'supply_chain_ci_permissions', 'description': 'CI workflows should use least-privilege tokens and avoid broad write permissions unless required.', 'remediation': 'Set explicit read-only defaults and grant write permissions only to jobs that publish trusted artifacts.'}, {'id': 'SCR-010', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'CI/CD Injection', 'name': 'Detect untrusted input reaching shell commands in CI', 'match_strategy': 'supply_chain_ci_injection', 'description': 'Pull request titles, branch names, issue text, commit messages, and other untrusted fields should not be interpolated directly into shell commands.', 'remediation': 'Pass untrusted values through environment variables, quote safely, validate inputs, or avoid shell evaluation.'}, {'id': 'SCR-011', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'Install Script Risk', 'name': 'Review package install scripts and lifecycle hooks', 'match_strategy': 'supply_chain_install_scripts', 'description': 'Package lifecycle scripts such as preinstall, install, postinstall, prepare, setup hooks, and build scripts can execute attacker-controlled code.', 'remediation': 'Disable scripts where possible, allowlist trusted packages, review lifecycle scripts, and run installs in constrained build environments.'}, {'id': 'SCR-012', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'Registry Trust', 'name': 'Enforce trusted package registries', 'match_strategy': 'supply_chain_registry_trust', 'description': 'Package managers and build tools should use approved registries and should not silently fall back to public or insecure registries.', 'remediation': 'Configure registry allowlists, private mirrors, TLS validation, authentication, and package scope routing.'}, {'id': 'SCR-013', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Maintainer Trust', 'name': 'Flag packages with unclear maintainer or source repository identity', 'match_strategy': 'supply_chain_maintainer_identity', 'description': 'Packages should have a clear publisher, source repository, and release process suitable for the trust level of the application.', 'remediation': 'Verify maintainer identity, project activity, source repository links, and release history before accepting the package.'}, {'id': 'SCR-014', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'Build Isolation', 'name': 'Build untrusted dependencies in isolated environments', 'match_strategy': 'supply_chain_build_isolation', 'description': 'Build steps that install or execute third-party code should run in isolated environments without long-lived secrets or broad network access.', 'remediation': 'Use ephemeral builders, scoped credentials, network egress controls, and secret minimization for dependency installation and build jobs.'}, {'id': 'SCR-015', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'Secret Exposure', 'name': 'Prevent release and build workflows from exposing secrets to untrusted code', 'match_strategy': 'supply_chain_secret_exposure', 'description': 'Workflows triggered from forks, pull requests, or untrusted branches should not expose deployment credentials, signing keys, or registry tokens.', 'remediation': 'Restrict secret access by event type, environment protection, branch protection, and manual approvals for privileged release jobs.'}, {'id': 'SCR-016', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Artifact Checksums', 'name': 'Verify downloaded artifacts before execution', 'match_strategy': 'supply_chain_unverified_download', 'description': 'Scripts should not download and execute remote artifacts without checksum, signature, digest, or pinned immutable source verification.', 'remediation': 'Pin artifact versions, verify checksums or signatures, and avoid pipe-to-shell installation patterns.'}, {'id': 'SCR-017', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'SBOM', 'name': 'Produce SBOMs for release artifacts', 'match_strategy': 'supply_chain_missing_sbom', 'description': 'Release artifacts and container images should have SBOMs so dependency content can be audited and monitored after release.', 'remediation': 'Generate CycloneDX or SPDX SBOMs during build and attach them to release or artifact metadata.'}, {'id': 'SCR-018', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'Branch and Tag Protection', 'name': 'Protect release branches and tags', 'match_strategy': 'supply_chain_unprotected_release_refs', 'description': 'Release branches and tags should require review, protected ref rules, and restricted write access to prevent artifact substitution.', 'remediation': 'Enable protected branches, protected tags, required reviews, status checks, and release environment approvals.'}, {'id': 'SCR-019', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Dependency Update Governance', 'name': 'Require review for dependency update automation', 'match_strategy': 'supply_chain_dependency_bot_governance', 'description': 'Automated dependency updates should not auto-merge into sensitive code or release branches without policy checks.', 'remediation': 'Require CI, approvals, semantic version policies, and security review for high-risk updates.'}, {'id': 'SCR-020', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'Build Reproducibility', 'name': 'Prefer reproducible builds for high-trust artifacts', 'match_strategy': 'supply_chain_reproducible_builds', 'description': 'High-trust release artifacts should be reproducible or otherwise verifiable against source and build provenance.', 'remediation': 'Pin build tools, isolate builders, record build parameters, and compare rebuild output or provenance attestations.'}], 'default_match_strategy': 'unspecified', 'report_template': '# Supply Chain Risk Report\n\n## Scope\n\n- Skill: `detect-supply-chain-risks`\n- Target: `{{target}}`\n- Date: `{{date}}`\n- Evidence reviewed: `{{evidence_summary}}`\n- Generated: `{{generated_at}}`\n\n## Summary\n\n| Severity | Findings | CI/CD | Dependencies | Containers | Artifacts | Registry |\n|----------|----------|------|--------------|------------|-----------|----------|\n| Critical | {{summary.critical.findings}} | {{summary.critical.cicd}} | {{summary.critical.dependencies}} | {{summary.critical.containers}} | {{summary.critical.artifacts}} | {{summary.critical.registry}} |\n| High | {{summary.high.findings}} | {{summary.high.cicd}} | {{summary.high.dependencies}} | {{summary.high.containers}} | {{summary.high.artifacts}} | {{summary.high.registry}} |\n| Medium | {{summary.medium.findings}} | {{summary.medium.cicd}} | {{summary.medium.dependencies}} | {{summary.medium.containers}} | {{summary.medium.artifacts}} | {{summary.medium.registry}} |\n| Low | {{summary.low.findings}} | {{summary.low.cicd}} | {{summary.low.dependencies}} | {{summary.low.containers}} | {{summary.low.artifacts}} | {{summary.low.registry}} |\n\n## Findings\n\n{{#each findings}}\n### {{id}} - {{name}}\n\n- Severity: {{severity}}\n- Category: {{category}}\n- Asset: `{{asset}}`\n- Evidence: `{{evidence}}`\n- Trust Boundary: {{trust_boundary}}\n- Attack Scenario: {{attack_scenario}}\n- Impact: {{impact}}\n- Remediation: {{remediation}}\n{{/each}}\n\n## Integrity and Provenance Gaps\n\n{{#each provenance_gaps}}\n- {{gap}}\n{{/each}}\n\n{{#if no_findings}}\nNo supply chain risk indicators were detected in the reviewed evidence.\n{{/if}}\n\n## Notes\n\nThis report identifies ways the build, dependency, release, or deployment chain can be tampered with. Known vulnerable package CVEs should be reported through `scan-sca-dependencies`.\n'}
